Q: &quot;Your site has no hreflang tags.&quot; [Google Webmastertools - International Targeting]. How to fix this error? A: <p>I can detect two errors in your configuration:</p>

<ol>
<li><p>You have put the <code>x-default</code> value in the <code>rel</code> parameter and it should be a value for the <code>hreflang</code> parameter.</p></li>
<li><p>You are specifying a different <code>x-default</code> value for each location.</p></li>
</ol>

<p>According to <a href="https://webmasters.googleblog.com/2013/04/x-default-hreflang-for-international-pages.html" rel="nofollow">Webmasters blog from Google</a>:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>The new x-default hreflang attribute value signals to our algorithms that this page doesn’t target any specific language or locale and is the default page when no other page is better suited.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>In your case, it looks that your default page is <a href="http://szerelemguru.ro/" rel="nofollow">http://szerelemguru.ro/</a> and such url should be the one with <code>hreflang="x-default"</code>.</p>

